  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Acting Now for Food Security and Resilient Food Systems - Ghana</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In this programme in Ghana, we support farmers from the Eastern, Ashanti, Ahafo, Northern Regions and Greater Accra region to produce more and better maize, rice and vegetables. We support them with better agricultural practices, better market connectivity, improved storage and food distribution systems and training in post-harvest management practices. We expect this to support production levels, reduce losses and enhance income from farming. Urban households will also be supported with knowledge and skills in home/kitchen gardens. Market linkages are also established with off-takers to enhance food distribution, besides linking producers with bio-fertilizer producers/suppliers to improve soil health for enhanced productivity. The Gender Action Learning methodology (GALS) and the Engaging Men through Accountable Practice (EMAP) methodology are employed to promote gender equality in the communities.</narrative>
  </description>
